{
  "id": "PPA-10",
  "title": "Biotic & Abiotic Stress Pathways",
  "subtitle": "Pattern-triggered immunity (PTI), MAPK cascades, CBF/DREB regulon, and heat shock factors",
  "caption": "Integrated plant defense and acclimation pathways. Plasma membrane pattern recognition receptors (FLS2/BAK1) perceive bacterial flagellin (flg22), activating BIK1 transphosphorylation and triggering the canonical MPK3/MPK6 signaling cascade. Concurrently, environmental temperature and osmotic fluctuations activate the CBF1-3/DREB regulon for cold/freezing tolerance and HSFA1/HSFA2 for heat shock protein (HSP70/90) chaperone induction.",
